### 2. `.gitignore`
This prevents Jupyter checkpoint folders, Python cache files, and Conda/virtual environment clutter from being uploaded when you run `git add .` in Git Bash. *(Note: Make sure the filename starts with a dot: `.gitignore`)*

```text
# Jupyter Notebook checkpoints
.ipynb_checkpoints/
*/.ipynb_checkpoints/*

# Python bytecode & cache
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class

# Virtual environments
venv/
env/
.venv/

# OS-generated files
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
